From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:58:50 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] ps1-options

For pcsx_rearmed only, slot answers every option key the core declares:
an explicit value wins (bios auto, so a missing BIOS falls back to HLE,
memcard1 libretro, memcard2 none, frameskip off, the NEON enhancement
off, threaded rendering and the dynarec thread auto), any other declared
key gets its declared default, and a key the core never declared is
still answered false. Every other core keeps upstream's answers. PS1
records no rewind and refuses the rewind gesture, and run-ahead stays
on mGBA only.

Answering the declared defaults follows oauramos/omega-zero, and the
threaded-rendering finding is AaronC1990/tray's (both GPL-3.0).
